{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1344088-doing-your-homework-with-magick","id":1344088,"title":"Doing your homework with Magick?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-27T16:47:53-07:00","id":1344088,"title":"Doing your homework with Magick?","content":"So, riffing off an older thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305131-spheres-for-computation-efffects\">Spheres for computational effects</a>... Say you have a PC student in High School or College/University. They are lousy at said subject, they have a challenging homework assignment and want to use magic instead. How would you adjudicate this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T05:58:49-07:00","id":1344172,"title":"","content":"Ask: What are you going to do with your magick to that effect, and how are you going to do it?<br /> <br /> To try to narrow what kind of Effect it's going to be casted, Spheres needed, and how to manifest it mechanically (as a bonus on some roll, the homework with the correct answers being summoned or automatically completed after the Arete roll, the answers manifesting in your head, etc). Several examples of how to adjudicate such a thing were menitoned in that thread.<br /> <br /> My main point would be to not limit this &quot;a priori&quot; to a single general concrete RAW that can be applied at all times (and almost certainly would end on &quot;increase your Inteligence&quot;/&quot;lower the difficulty&quot;, which reduces the so-called versatility of magick to <i>just two effects</i>, mechanically speaking), but rather adjudicate basing on how the spell it's defined. To recapitulate my opinion from the mentioned thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I think that converting that to a -3 it's kinda booring and not the only option. One should use the rules that are better to model the narrative of the spell. Summoning the homework of a good student and copying it with Matter, for instance, wouldn't fall under &quot;magic enhancing abilities&quot; rules but under conjuration and transmutation rules.<br /> <br /> The rules mentioned in the spellcasting section don't cover everything that should be used to model a spell and the ST is encouraged to get creative at that point. RAW you can always go the the general table of &quot;Magickal Feats&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-28-2019, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T14:02:24-07:00","id":1344498,"title":"","content":"Like Aleph said, you an do a ton of stuff with Magick and it won't be the same.<br /> <br /> For your answer: Really it depends on the spheres. I could see a ton of spheres helping with this.<br /> <br /> Either using Mind/Spirit/Correspondence magick to contact some entity that represents the vague concept of homework (or possibly cheating/the subject at hand) could give you the answer to the problem. You could use the previous spheres as well to simply read someones mind and find the answer, contact a spirit that knows the answer and ask (As opposed to literally just mentally contacting /the answer in spirit form/ and writing it down), or anything like that.<br /> <br /> You could use mind to do the previously mentioned INT boost to just use your own knowledge in the process.<br /> <br /> If the homework is digital you could probably some some silly shit with Data","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:17:37-07:00","id":1345392,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Use Spirit to summon a spirit of knowledge, asking it to provide the answers.</li> <li>Use Matter to &quot;read&quot; the answers on someone else's homework, and then rearrange the material on your submission so it has their answers.</li> <li>If the teacher/professor marks up homework, you can use Time 2 + Matter 2 to look into the assignment's future and read how the answers are graded (which ones are marked correct or incorrect, etc). Then adjust the answers until you predict a perfect score. Doesn't work on all formats of homework.</li> <li>Affix a Mind effect onto the homework (probably locked with Matter) to convince anyone who reads it that the answers are correct. Basically, you're trying low-key mind control on the teacher/professor to make them think you did the work.</li> <li>Go to the teacher/professor after class and start asking them questions about the homework assignment. Have a running Mind 2 effect that lets you probe their surface thoughts, so when you prompt them with a question they begin thinking about the answer.</li> <li>Trade your magick skills for the aid of people who know the subject. For example, for Physics homework, find a physicist with poor health and cure them with Life, in return for the physicist doing your work for you. This is pretty Vulgar and liable to attract attention if you can't swear the &quot;helper&quot; to secrecy. But if you help them well, most people would be willing to stay quiet. This is also a decent - if risky - way to start a Cult. Alternatively, there are a lot of really smart Awakened people, who might be willing to trade a little intellectual grunt work for magickal favors.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}